{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/173445-the-battle-wheel-vs-ticks","id":173445,"title":"The Battle Wheel vs. ticks","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-18T18:38:09-07:00","id":173445,"title":"The Battle Wheel vs. ticks","content":"When I first began playing Scion, I instantly fell in love with the Battle Wheel System. Mostly because it did what no other world of darkness game had done so far:<br /> It made for fun combat!<br /> <br /> now, after playing for quite some time, I found out that the battle wheel only had 12 positions. Since I wrote a program to handle this for me, this never occured to me. Thus, we had a lot of people doing things that took far longer than that and we've had extremely lucky rolls pushing opponents to 15 ticks or so until their next move thanks to some homebrew knacks.<br /> <br /> We simply moved everybody a step closer to &quot;their turn&quot; every tick.<br /> <br /> Has anybody else extended the Battle Wheel like this? What did you feel were the pros and cons of this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/593-gemstone","name":"Gemstone","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T21:46:33-07:00","id":173702,"title":"","content":"I think I'm always going to be a fan of a simple initiative based turn system. Something that could be a cool addition would be more mechanical ways to make people move around in the initiative order, that way a bad roll at the start of a fight doesn't leave you at the end of the pack, and you can bring down somebody who rolls really well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T11:54:59-07:00","id":174404,"title":"","content":"No character can begin combat later than tick six by RAW. I use the Tick System for combat, but not the Battle Wheel.<br /> I just write down the current tick, and whenever someone takes an action I change their number to reflect the new tick.<br /> For example: Bob = 6. When the current tick becomes 6, Bob takes a speed 4 action. Bob = 10.<br /> <br /> <i>This lets me keep track of exactly how many ticks every combat has.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T15:13:19-07:00","id":174611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/173445-the-battle-wheel-vs-ticks?p=174404#post174404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No character can begin combat later than tick six by RAW. I use the Tick System for combat, but not the Battle Wheel.<br /> I just write down the current tick, and whenever someone takes an action I change their number to reflect the new tick.<br /> For example: Bob = 6. When the current tick becomes 6, Bob takes a speed 4 action. Bob = 10.<br /> <br /> <i>This lets me keep track of exactly how many ticks every combat has.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, seems i was unclear. the starting position can be no higher than 6, however, we have some custom knacks that makes it possible to shift around someone's position in the tick que. We also have a few boons for this.<br /> <br /> Do you allow anyone to be pushed beyond 12 ticks?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":593,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/593-gemstone","user":"Gemstone","date":". 06-20-2014, 04:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/593-gemstone","name":"Gemstone","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T20:11:15-07:00","id":174875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gemstone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/173445-the-battle-wheel-vs-ticks?p=174611#post174611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah, seems i was unclear. the starting position can be no higher than 6, however, we have some custom knacks that makes it possible to shift around someone's position in the tick que. We also have a few boons for this.<br /> <br /> DO you allow anyone to be pushed beyond 12 ticks?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, mostly because we run our games online and even when people are seperated by a few ticks, it translates to a very long downtime between folks' turns. 12 tick pushback is brutal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T09:31:17-07:00","id":175296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gemstone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/173445-the-battle-wheel-vs-ticks?p=174611#post174611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you allow anyone to be pushed beyond 12 ticks?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. There have been cases where a character showed up late to the fight, had to roll his join battle, and was then placed 0-6 Ticks from the Current Tick. But I run combats fast and brutal most of the time, and combats rarely take more than 30 ticks in total unless I am running a showcase fight or intentionally including time lapses.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T17:33:59-07:00","id":175653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aynie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/173445-the-battle-wheel-vs-ticks?p=174875#post174875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> No, mostly because we run our games online and even when people are seperated by a few ticks, it translates to a very long downtime between folks' turns. 12 tick pushback is brutal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, we usually run ticks very fast mostly because we've mechanized a lot of the die rolling for opponents and such with functions I've created. We usually have combat with a lot of lesser foes and are thus required to make many rolls quickly. Then again, we do run our own homebrew version of the combat rules and have severely limited the usage of &quot;monkey in the middle&quot;.<br /> <br /> [quote:Iry]No. There have been cases where a character showed up late to the fight, had to roll his join battle, and was then placed 0-6 Ticks from the Current Tick. But I run combats fast and brutal most of the time, and combats rarely take more than 30 ticks in total unless I am running a showcase fight or intentionally including time lapses.[/quote]<br /> Ah. The longest fight we've had ran up to... I think something around 150-300 ticks, mostly because it was the final showdown between a massive party of 9 scions vs. a titanic horde of underworld monsters.<br /> <br /> Have you made any rulings to simplify or alter the use of ticks?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/593-gemstone","name":"Gemstone","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T12:14:17-07:00","id":194875,"title":"","content":"Captain self-promotion to the rescue!!!<br /> <br /> Edit: I used the add link buton but nothing shows up. Here's an online wheel I wrote and have been using for years: <a href=\"http://rpg-tools.org/generators/tools/wheel/wheelWithSharing.php\" target=\"_blank\">http://rpg-tools.org/generators/tool...ithSharing.php</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Need some online tools, including a Scion/Exalted battle wheel? <a href=\"http://rpg-tools.org/generators/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">http://rpg-tools.org/generators/index.php</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/829-james-mcmurray","name":"James McMurray","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}